# virtualenv and caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# One deliberate exception: real-circuit CSVs downloaded by
# physics/tracks_data.py (TRACKS.md staging step 3). TUM's racetrack-database
# is LGPL-3.0 over OpenStreetMap data (ODbL, share-alike) -- vendoring the
# files would pull that share-alike chain into this repo. TRACKS.md §3's own
# licensing survey recommends a downloader instead, so the CSVs are fetched
# on first use and cached here, never committed. Only our own converter code
# (physics/tracks_data.py) is tracked.
physics/tracks_cache/

# Nothing else is ignored on purpose.
#
# Generated outputs ARE committed: experiments/*/out/ and diagnostics/out/ hold the
# figures and results.json every episode draft cites. The articles reference them by
# path, so a checkout without them has broken links and unverifiable numbers. They
# are regenerable — that is what each run.py is for — but the point of committing
# them is that you can read the series without a solver licence or an hour of CPU.
experiments/ep10/out/morph_frames/
